<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles-Denis Bourbaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1897</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles-Denis Bourbaki was a French general of Greek descent who commanded the Imperial Guard in 1870 and then the Army of the East in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>. After failing to relieve Belfort, his defeated army of about 87,000 men crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in February 1871, where it was disarmed and interned, an event depicted in the Bourbaki Panorama at Lucerne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-denis-bourbaki.jpg" alt="Charles-Denis Bourbaki" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre-Louis Pierson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_Bourbaki.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
